From f93c8f1c7b5baa4d603d59d6a55d08e401767ac6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 13:56:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 36/75] AlarmManagerService: make the ALARM_EVENT soft-alarm
 path deliver listener alarms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the ARC container the kernel wakealarm is unavailable: timerfd_create with
CLOCK_BOOTTIME_ALARM / CLOCK_REALTIME_ALARM gates on capable(CAP_WAKE_ALARM)
against the init user namespace, which a capability held only in the container's
child userns does not satisfy — so the syscall returns EPERM, the native
AlarmManagerService.init() fails (mNativeData==0), and the AlarmThread falls back
to the ALARM_EVENT software-simulation path.

Stock's fallback loop only delivered PendingIntent (operation) alarms and
unconditionally called getAlarmOperationBundle()/alarm.operation.send(), so it
NPE'd on the first listener alarm — the per-minute TIME_TICK — crash-looping
system_server ~60s into boot, on the minute.

Deliver through the standard deliverAlarmsLocked() instead (under mLock, as the
native path does). It dispatches both operation and listener alarms via
mDeliveryTracker and catches per-alarm failures, so the soft alarm becomes the
supported delivery path. WAKE_UP alarms only fire while awake (no suspend
wakeups), which is fine here — Chrome OS owns power/suspend and the ARC power
bridge handles time-sensitive wakeups.

Verified on device: 0 getAlarmOperationBundle NPEs, system_server survives
past the TIME_TICK fires (uptime > 60s/120s), boot completes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I893855d53e3bae214618aaab5550108f94f406d2
---
 .../server/alarm/AlarmManagerService.java     | 32 ++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/apex/jobscheduler/service/java/com/android/server/alarm/AlarmManagerService.java b/apex/jobscheduler/service/java/com/android/server/alarm/AlarmManagerService.java
index f1a39310e2f8..69504cbe5b72 100644
--- a/apex/jobscheduler/service/java/com/android/server/alarm/AlarmManagerService.java
+++ b/apex/jobscheduler/service/java/com/android/server/alarm/AlarmManagerService.java
@@ -4915,25 +4915,19 @@ public class AlarmManagerService extends SystemService {
                         final long nowELAPSED = mInjector.getElapsedRealtime();
                         triggerAlarmsLocked(triggerList, nowELAPSED);
                         updateNextAlarmClockLocked();
-                    }
-
-                    // now trigger the alarms without the lock held
-                    for (int i = 0; i < triggerList.size(); i++) {
-                        Alarm alarm = triggerList.get(i);
-                        try {
-                            // Disallow AlarmManager to start random background activity.
-                            final Bundle bundle = getAlarmOperationBundle(alarm);
-                            alarm.operation.send(/* context */ null, /* code */0, /* intent */
-                                    null, /* onFinished */null, /* handler */
-                                    null, /* requiredPermission */ null, bundle);
-                        } catch (PendingIntent.CanceledException e) {
-                            if (alarm.repeatInterval > 0) {
-                                // This IntentSender is no longer valid, but this
-                                // is a repeating alarm, so toss the hoser.
-                                removeImpl(alarm.operation, null);
-                            }
-                        }
-                        decrementAlarmCount(alarm.uid, 1);
+                        // fydroid/ARC: this software-simulation path is the LIVE alarm
+                        // delivery path in the container — the kernel wakealarm is
+                        // unavailable (timerfd CLOCK_*_ALARM needs CAP_WAKE_ALARM in the
+                        // init user namespace, which a container-userns cap does not
+                        // satisfy), so mNativeData==0 and AlarmThread falls back here.
+                        // The original inline loop only delivered PendingIntent
+                        // (operation) alarms and NPE'd on listener alarms (e.g. the
+                        // per-minute TIME_TICK), crash-looping system_server. Deliver via
+                        // the standard deliverAlarmsLocked(), which dispatches BOTH
+                        // operation and listener alarms (and catches per-alarm failures).
+                        // Note: WAKE_UP alarms only fire while the device is awake (no
+                        // suspend wakeups) — acceptable here as Chrome OS owns power.
+                        deliverAlarmsLocked(triggerList, nowELAPSED);
                     }
                     break;
                 }
